rce_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[routing_anti_patterns_registry].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"world_model_projection_drift_control_room","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[world_model_projection_drift_control_room].axiom_refs"}],"cited_by_count":32,"component_ids":["batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule","batch10_governance_compilers_capsule","batch10_live_source_drift_capsule","batch11_saturation_engines_capsule","batch12_market_dashboard_read_model_capsule","batch12_prediction_market_board_capsule","batch4_proof_authority_runtime","batch5_authority_systems_capsule","batch6_unsurfaced_primitives_capsule","batch7_demo_take_console_capsule","batch7_macro_engines_capsule","batch7_oracle_sibling_capsule","batch7_secondary_runtime_capsule","batch8_audio_level_rms_port","batch8_compliance_pipeline_capsule","batch8_policy_engines_capsule","batch8_structural_theses_capsule","batch8_tools_tail_primitives_capsule","batch8_validator_checker_capsule","batch9_macro_engines_capsule","bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","cognitive_operator_registry","cold_reader_route_map","durable_agent_work_landing_replay","engine_room_demo","macro_projection_import_protocol","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","public_reveal_walkthrough","routing_anti_patterns_registry","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":["AP-4","AP-12","AP-13","AP-17"],"id":"AX-4","kind":"axiom","plain":"Formal clause: for derived artifact `a=f(B)`, identity is `H(B)`; equal basis may reuse, basis drift forces recompute, and missing basis is bottom.","principles":["P-5","P-14","P-15","P-17"],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The pharmacy only describes one counter that checks orders; some reuse paths in the system still need the same check added.","maps":[{"analogy":"the medicine identified by the exact current order it was filled from","doctrine":"the result identified by a hash of its inputs"},{"analogy":"an unchanged order lets the same refill be dispensed","doctrine":"matching inputs allow reuse"},{"analogy":"a changed order needs a newly issued prescription","doctrine":"changed inputs force a recompute"},{"analogy":"if no order can be found, nothing is dispensed","doctrine":"missing inputs mean no result"},{"analogy":"your name on file is different from a matching current order","doctrine":"a matching name or path is different from matching inputs"}],"text":"A pharmacy refills a prescription only against the doctor's current order, whatever name is on file. If the order changed it must be issued again, and if no order can be found you get nothing."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A pipeline serves a cached output because the requested name matches an earlier run, although the inputs that produced it have since changed.","does_not_prove":"The named import and work-landing steps compare hashes; other reuse paths in the system are covered only if they do the same, and one required error code for work landing is still recorded as unfinished.","enforced_in_component_ids":["macro_projection_import_protocol","durable_agent_work_landing_replay"],"example":{"component_ids":["macro_projection_import_protocol"],"text":"The source-import protocol brings non-secret files in with a manifest of their hashes, and refuses to reuse an imported copy when the source hash no longer matches, so a changed input cannot pass as an unchanged result."},"governs":"When a cached or reused result may stand in for a fresh computation.","plain":"A stored result can be reused only when the exact inputs it was built from are unchanged; a matching name or location is not enough. If the inputs changed it must be rebuilt, and if they cannot be found there is no result.","potential_misread":"That a matching name or file name makes it safe to reuse a stored result, so checking the inputs again is wasted effort.","refuses":"Reusing a cached result by name after its inputs have changed.","requires":"A declared list of inputs, an identity computed as a hash of those inputs, and a hash comparison that decides between reuse and recompute.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"A stale or tampered result cannot pass as fresh just because its name or path matched."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"AXIOMS.md::AX-4","statement":"Formal clause: for derived artifact `a=f(B)`, identity is `H(B)`; equal basis\nmay reuse, basis drift forces recompute, and missing basis is bottom.\n\nLineage: referential transparency, Merkle/content-addressed storage, hermetic\nbuilds.\n\nRoute: recorded as strongly witnessed by `durable_agent_work_landing_replay`,\n`macro_projection_import_protocol`, `command_run_singleflight.py` and the Crown\nJewel source-manifest checks. The tests reject a run whose source digest or\nfreshness inputs do not match the recorded ones. One layer-debt receipt is\nopen: a semantic freshness code that has not yet been written out as exact\npublic code.\n\nAnti-axiom: a cached result is reused by name after its inputs have changed.","statement_sha256":"25245a9b4dd95c5fe48bd026b987fc6e3a692437a7036fe1453cc41e689f806c","title":"Content-addressed determinism","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}